    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it feels more than just \"empty\" though. it feels like a mistake. like the world is trying to force this hollow thing to keep taking up space when the essence of what made life worth it is completely extinguished. why does the machine have to keep running if the pilot is gone? it feels so illogical to just keep dragging this broken machinery around when there's nothing left to guide it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
